[size=5][b]Marriage Calculation Assistant[/b][/size]

[size=5][b]At a glance[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]🟢 [b]Version 3.1.0[/b] · Targets CK3 [b]1.20.0.3[/b].
[*]🟢 [b]Standalone:[/b] no other mod required. Parley is optional.
[*]🟢 [b]Candidate scores, hover breakdowns and optional score sorting[/b] in the marriage picker.
[*]🟢 [b]Nine languages:[/b] English, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Russian, Simplified Chinese and Spanish.
[*]🔴 [b]Scores measure candidate gameplay potential[/b], not AI acceptance or a particular marriage's outcome.
[*]🔴 [b]Marriage-window conflict:[/b] another mod replacing [b]gui/interaction_marriage.gui[/b] needs a functional compatibility patch.
[*]🔴 [b]Puppet arrangements use the native list[/b], without MCA scores or MCA sorting. Current AGOT compatibility is on hold.
[*]🔴 [b]Multiplayer is unverified.[/b]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Find the person behind the list[/b][/size]

A useful claim, an exceptional mind or a powerful ally: find promising names in a long marriage list and see what makes them stand out.

[size=5][b]Compare candidates without losing the details[/b][/size]

Hover an [b]MCA[/b] score for its component breakdown. Choose [b]MCA: by score[/b] to bring the highest-scoring candidates to the top.

Compare candidates from other courts or your own, using the same core weights. Adapters can add setting-specific opportunities.

Scores do not change acceptance or modify candidates. MCA points are separate from Parley's treaty score.

[size=5][b]What the score includes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Visible inheritable qualities:[/b] intelligence, beauty and physique tiers receive +10, +20 and +30; negative counterparts subtract the same amounts. Other supported active inheritable traits have their own weights. Hidden/recessive genetics are not inspected.
[*][b]Skills:[/b] up to 30 points from five public skills and the standard assist-spouse contribution. Effective age below 16 or incapability gives zero. This does not assume eligibility to serve on your council.
[*][b]Age-based reproductive potential:[/b] a 0–20 index of effective age and visible restrictions, not birth probability. A child's zero describes current potential, not lifelong childlessness.
[*][b]Dynastic prestige potential:[/b] −5 to +45 from the dynasty marriage-prestige table: dynastic standing, not the pair's exact reward.
[*][b]Explicit claims:[/b] the strongest contributes up to 24; pressed claims weigh twice as much as unpressed claims of the same rank. Marriage does not immediately transfer claims or titles.
[*][b]Potential alliance:[/b] up to 100 from the ally's military strength relative to yours, only when the native row reports it. Assistance is not guaranteed.
[/list]

Components and adapter contributions add up to the score. These are comparison weights, not percentages or a shared resource. Inspect the breakdown for what matters to your plans.

Court position, arranger opinion, reluctance to release courtiers, hidden fertility/health, secret parentage, predicted children, succession queues and the selected couple's full value are outside the model.

[size=5][b]How to use it[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Open a marriage picker and set the game's normal filters.
[*]Hover an [b]MCA[/b] number to inspect its components.
[*]Close the filter panel and choose [b]MCA: by score[/b] for descending score order. Equal scores keep their current native order; unavailable scores go last.
[*]Choose [b]Default list[/b] to restore the native ordering and filter controls.
[/list]

The pinned-player row stays pinned. Changing picker side, marriage type or candidate context clears the sorted snapshot. Selecting a moved row selects its displayed character.

MCA scores and sorting apply when arranging as your own ruler. Switching to a puppet clears the sorted snapshot and uses CK3's native list without MCA scores or sorting.

[size=5][b]Compatibility and load order[/b][/size]

[b]Vanilla file replacement:[/b] [b]gui/interaction_marriage.gui[/b]. MCA supplies its own score interface, sorting and cleanup. It does not replace [b]gui/shared/lists.gui[/b], [b]arrange_marriage_interaction[/b] or [b]marry_off_interaction[/b].

Another [b]gui/interaction_marriage.gui[/b] replacement needs a functional patch; load order cannot merge files. A mod changing only [b]gui/shared/lists.gui[/b] can work if its row retains vanilla's [b]character_relation[/b] block in the name/age column. This is not blanket list-mod compatibility.

[b]Optional combined load order:[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Parley: The Negotiating Table
[*]Marriage Calculation Assistant
[/list]

Standalone: enable MCA alone.

[b]AGOT compatibility is on hold[/b] pending upstream CK3 1.20 support and fresh combined checks. Earlier AGOT setups do not apply to this release.

[b]Held adapter:[/b] [url=https://github.com/G4VV4KH/-CK3-AGOT-Marriage-Calculation-Assistant]AGOT: Marriage Calculation Assistant[/url] adds current-dragonrider potential without a replacement GUI. No additional interface patches are included. Enable one copy of each mod.

[size=5][b]Saves and known limits[/b][/size]

Sorting stores a temporary snapshot on the local player; picker cleanup removes it. [b]Close the marriage picker before saving or disabling MCA[/b], or inert snapshot variables can remain.

Screenshots show [b]MCA 3.0.1 on CK3 1.19.0.6[/b]; some interface details may differ.

Advancing time with a sorted picker open, reloading an active snapshot, multiplayer and other total conversions remain unverified.

[size=5][b]Feedback and support[/b][/size]

For score reports, include the candidate, breakdown, picker side, versions, load order and a screenshot; add resolution and UI scale for interface problems.

